  "description": "SGU Hackx 1.0 is a 36-hour national-level hackathon organized by the School of Computer Applications, SDGI Global University , in collaboration with TechSpire Global Technologies . The hackathon brings together passionate students, developers, innovators, and problem-solvers to build innovative technology-driven solutions to real-world challenges. Participants will work in teams, develop their ideas, and showcase their projects before a panel of judges. What to Expect: 36 hours of continuous innovation and development Real-world problem statements Team-based coding and solution building Mentorship and technical guidance Project evaluation by industry/academic experts Networking with fellow innovators Certificates and exciting prizes Opportunity to showcase your project on a national platform Theme: Innovation • Technology • Problem Solving • Entrepreneurship Get ready to code, create, collaborate, and compete at SGU HACKX 1.0.",
